/**
 * THE VESSELS, PAINTED
 *
 * All seven, cut from supplied sheets and keyed at build time — the first six
 * off a cream ground (flood from the cell edges, rim un-mixed from the cream, or
 * each one wears a pale halo on the dark room), the Cedar Tray off flat magenta,
 * which is the easier key and why every sheet since has used it.
 *
 * The tray comes in two states because a painting cannot open its own lid:
 * `koji_tray` is the bare bed and `koji_tray_open` has the lid propped, which is
 * what keeps `lidOpen` meaning something now that the drawing is gone.
 *
 * WebP with alpha, all eight in 102 KB. Data URIs because the published
 * page's CSP blocks external images. A painting never takes the ink filter; see
 * `.iso-lift.painted`.
 */
